+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** The Odin v2 build looks flat/scribbled next to the UE slice-1 reference (user verdict after playing both: "doesn't look as good as expected out of the box"). The UE slice-1 look-parity checklist hit ✅ on palette, ribbon roads (casing + rounded caps), soft blob shadows, AA, and eased motion; the Odin build has the palette + easing but MISSING ribbon casing, heavy 33%-alpha shadows, and plain packet dots.
+
+**Approach:** A presentation-only polish pass that closes the gap against the UE slice-1 recipe (match the FEEL, never pixel-copy a different renderer): (1) modest warm-cream canvas lift toward the UE #F5F0E4; (2) ribbon ROAD CASING — a slightly wider, darker under-stroke with rounded caps under every pipe band (the UE "casing border + fill" read) so pipes read as engineered ribbons instead of chalk lines; (3) soft blob shadows — retune the node contact shadow to the UE "oversized low-alpha rounded blob offset 2-3px" recipe (softer + larger + closer); (4) packet-dot polish — a small warm-cream glint highlight (the flat-2D car read), size + easing untouched (the 7.1 base must not regress). All changes are draw-time only (ODN-1): no sim, no serialization, no LOG_VERSION, no catalog edits.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Presentation-only [ODN-1]: the sim spine, serialization, LOG_VERSION, packet contracts, routing semantics UNTOUCHED. No new sim state, no RNG, no transcendentals in the rasterized path (the §10.4 rule — new draw math is integer + IEEE f32).
+- Deterministic from (tick, seed, topology): every new visual is a pure function of existing inputs — same inputs → same pixels (the T2 spine).
+- T2 goldens re-bless deliberately with the honest process: rebuild `bin/harness` BEFORE bless, cause-document every shift in the PR, `cmp -l` every `.log.bin` vs HEAD (T1 must be byte-identical — only the standard version-field bytes may differ), splice/verify the catalog hash, update the palcheck pinned constants in the same PR.
+- The 7.1 easing/motion base is untouchable — packets keep their eased inter-snapshot lerp + lane speeds (no regression).
+- The user is ACTIVELY PLAYING the build (`odin run app`): every push leaves `odin build app` compiling and runnable.
+- New visual constants live render-side (the PULSE16/ROUTER_TIER_SCALE precedent) or in `data/palette.json` (cosmetic data, ODN-5) — never in the catalogs (cat.hash is golden-poison).
+- The 7.5 shipped verdict stands: `route_wires=false`, `wire_anchors=false` — the straight render remains the blessed default. The casing must ALSO apply in the 7.5 path-variant draw (consistency when a future gate flips a flag), but the shipped pixels are the straight branch.
+- palcheck's a11y oracle + mode tables stay green (the base palette change must keep every mode table passing — the tables themselves are untouched byte-for-byte).
+
+**Ask First:** none — the aesthetic verdict is the USER's at the mandatory lavish gallery gate (the briefing's bake-off: looks are the criterion, the human is the judge); the gate iterates until an explicit approve.
+
+**Never:** No gameplay/canon-surface changes, no catalog edits, no LOG_VERSION bump, no serialization change, no sprite/asset regeneration (the committed sprite pipeline is untouched), no new node types, no pipe-color meaning change (tier colors stay load-bearing — white roads from the UE fixture are NOT adopted; the tier identity is canon here).
+
