+## Design Notes
+
+- **Why casing, not pipe shadows:** the UE slice-1 recipe puts shadows under NODES only (roads are flat ribbons with casing). Pipe shadows would need translucent LINE draws — rlsw line primitives render OPAQUE regardless of alpha (the 7.1 field note), so a soft pipe shadow would diverge between the GPU app and the goldens. The casing is an OPAQUE solid (no alpha), so it is golden-safe by construction. Draw order: casing (wider, darker) → band → lane stripes → (halo on congestion) — the rim peeks ~2.25px each side.
+- **The canvas lift is modest on purpose:** #E8DDC2 → ~#EDE2C8 keeps the warm family + the map-token contrast (palcheck's pairwise separation under the a11y oracle: cream vs water/park/coast stays ≫ the 40 threshold). The UE #F5F0E4 is not adopted verbatim — our canvas also carries the landmass + grid contrast, and the established look-book §2 canon is user-approved; the lift is a step toward the UE whitespace read, not a re-theme.
+- **Re-bless honesty:** each of the 4 code commits carries its own deliberate re-bless (shadows → roads → palette → packets) so every commit stays CI-green; the PR cause-documents each shift with the diff-bundle bbox evidence (goldens/_reports). The `.log.bin`/`.t1` byte-compare is the T1 proof.
+
